 §5","norm_id":"n1f06d917fbbcb010","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Executor completes scripts+terraform+tests but has no named file to write the runbook into, or writes it where reviewers won't find it"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add to Design §5 the runbook artifact (e.g. the ADR-0112 runbook or a docs/runbooks/*.md path) and state AC8's proving check as a grep for the cap/alarm/remediation sections in that file.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"missing_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"missing_required_child","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["3 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Ground the journald restart-safety claim (socket activation + fd-store stream restoration across restart) in a citable source — e.g. sd_notify(3)/systemd.socket(5)/journald FDSTORE semantics — or downgrade the claim and treat the restart as potentially stream-affecting.","cohort":["T3"],"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.9,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'journald's sockets are PID-1-activated and its stdout stream fds live in the service's fd store and are restored, so no service goes down or loses its log stream'","Grounding section cites journald.conf(5) and systemd-journald.service(8) for the cap and ExecReload claims but NOT for the fd-store/socket-activation restart-survival behavior","If wrong, an --install-triggered restart could drop container stdout log streams mid-operation — the exact collateral class the S2 lesson (avoiding a docker restart) exists to prevent"],"finding":"The core restart-safety claim — that restarting systemd-journald loses no service's log stream because its sockets are PID-1 socket-activated and its stdout stream fds live in the service fd store and are restored — is asserted but grounded in no cited source, unlike every other systemd capability claim in the plan (which cite journald.conf(5) / systemd-journald.service(8)). This capability is what makes the whole 'restart is safe here where restart docker was not' design defensible.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f897dfc1bb2936f69","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Design §2 (Activation is OBSERVED)","norm_id":"n3a4fd56a53d0ab92","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["--install detects a changed drop-in on a busy box and restarts systemd-journald; if fds are not in fact restored, compose services momentarily lose their journal stream or a socket connection is dropped"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add to the Grounding section the specific systemd reference for FileDescriptorStoreMax / FDSTORE fd preservation and PID-1 socket activation of systemd-journald's sockets, matching how the ExecReload and SystemMaxUse claims are already cited.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.85,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"insufficient","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Verify `journalctl --vacuum-size=` (and any companion --vacuum-time/--vacuum-files the runbook uses) against journalctl(1)/--help and cite it in Grounding, classifying the surface as MATCH.","cohort":["T3"],"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.9,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC8: 'remediation (`journalctl --vacuum-size=`)'","The Grounding section cites journald.conf(5) and systemd-journald.service(8) but does not cite journalctl(1) or verify the --vacuum-size flag","Runbook commands are consumed under incident pressure, so a silent flag error is discovered at the worst time"],"finding":"AC8 names `journalctl --vacuum-size=` as the remediation the runbook must document, but the plan never verifies this subcommand/flag against journalctl --help; no other section grounds it. A flag-level mismatch (e.g. wrong form of the vacuum option) would ship a runbook that fails at the moment an operator needs it during disk pressure.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f9d45201a66f3eb84","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"AC8 and Design §5 remediation","norm_id":"n97eda7e58dc6b33f","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Operator follows the runbook during journal saturation and the documented journalctl invocation errors on an unrecognized flag"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2857,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"low","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}}],"impact_model_version":"plan-v5","material_fingerprint":"96841f36db75bacb","material_parts":{"children":["647ea2107ca5072f",0],"description":["4e1069fafd1b02f2",7992],"description_boxes":["670af646a34cdc2a",0],"file_impact":["3b0b33015d5514dd",8],"ticket_id":["42e811a4